fp-listen
=========

fp-listen, the FreshPorts daemon that listens for database notifications
and clears caches. Built and distributed as the FreeBSD package
py-freshports-fp-listen (port: FreshPorts/ports py-freshports-fp-listen).

This repository was split out of FreshPorts/daemontools, which was itself
converted from the daemontools project in the freshports-1 Subversion
repository (svn+ssh://svn.int.unixathome.org/freshports-1). README.md in
FreshPorts/daemontools describes that conversion. The split is done by
split-daemontools.sh in ~/src/freshports/git-conversion/.

It replaces an earlier conversion, now FreshPorts/archive.fp-listen. Despite
its name, that one held all of daemontools as of 2024-11-07, with SVN's
trunk/, branches/ and tags/ as plain directories and no git tags. Its
fp-listen content is identical to this repository's: branches/git/fp-listen
matches main, trunk/fp-listen matches trunk, and the same 58 SVN revisions
changed fp-listen in both. The one difference is fp-listen-1.0.1, which
there still holds the nested copy described below.


Where the code lived
--------------------

fp-listen was added as daemontools/trunk/fp-listen in r3765 (2006-09-07)
and kept that name. When branches/git was created from trunk in r5376
(2020-07-03), development continued on both:

  branch   daemontools path            SVN revisions
  ------   -------------------------   --------------------------------
  main     branches/git/fp-listen      r3765 - r6116 (2006 - 2024-11-07)
  trunk    trunk/fp-listen             r3765 - r5817 (2006 - 2021-09-10)

The two share history up to r5375. Each commit keeps only fp-listen/,
moved to the top of the repository; commits that did not touch it are
dropped. Every commit keeps its git-svn-id: trailer, giving the original
Subversion path and revision.


Tags
----

There are three lines of releases. The two older lines both have a 1.0.x
series, so they keep their SVN names; only the current line uses plain
version numbers, which is what a port with USE_GITHUB expects.

  trunk line, 2017-10-11 .. 2021-09-10, 21 tags, names unchanged:
      fp-listen-1.0.0 .. fp-listen-1.3.4

  git line, 2021-01-08 .. 2023-10-24, 10 tags, names unchanged:
      fp-listen-git-1.0.0 .. fp-listen-git-1.0.9

  current line, 2024-11-07, 3 tags, prefix dropped:
      fp-listen-2.0.0 .. 2.0.2   ->   2.0.0 .. 2.0.2

The trunk line has no fp-listen-1.0.2; none was made in SVN.

Each tag is annotated with the tagger, date and message of the SVN
revision that created it, and points at the commit for the revision it was
copied from. Its tree was checked to be identical to the corresponding tag
in FreshPorts/daemontools before it was created.

Corrections carried over from the conversion:

  - fp-listen-git-1.0.0 was created in r5570 by renaming the misnamed
    fp-listen-git1.0.0 ("Properly name this tag"). Its contents are
    branches/git/fp-listen at r5568.
  - fp-listen-1.0.1 (created r4863) is the release as created. In r4895 a
    second svn copy onto the existing tag nested a copy, fp-listen/, inside
    it; that nested copy is not included.


Releasing
---------

Previously cut-fp-listen.sh (in packaging-for-svn) tagged a release in
SVN, exported it, and copied the tarball to pkg01. With this repository a
release is a git tag named for the version; the port can fetch it with:

  USE_GITHUB=	yes
  GH_ACCOUNT=	FreshPorts
  GH_PROJECT=	fp-listen


Not converted
-------------

  - svn:ignore properties; there is no .gitignore.
  - $Id$ keywords, which remain unexpanded as stored in SVN.
